Adds getters for what the built-in certificate verification of an SSL uses, so
that it can be reproduced outside the handshake, e.g. on another thread from a
custom verify callback:

- SSL_get0_verify_cert_store: the X509_STORE the SSL verifies against (its
  verify store, or else the certificate store of its SSL_CTX).
- SSL_CTX_get_cert_verify_callback and X509_STORE_get_verify_cb: callbacks
  that take part in that verification. They may look up the SSL, so a
  verification elsewhere cannot run them.
- SSL_new_peer_chain_verify_ctx: builds the X509_STORE_CTX itself, sharing
  ssl_crypto_x509_session_verify_cert_chain's own init_peer_verify_ctx helper
  (extracted from it, not reimplemented) for the store/purpose/param/ECH-name
  setup and the same callback checks as above, so a future change to the
  built-in's setup cannot silently diverge from this. Returns NULL, queuing no
  error, when a callback is set; the result otherwise only borrows ssl's
  current store and chain, like X509_STORE_CTX_init itself, so a caller that
  needs it to outlive ssl (e.g. to move verification to another thread) must
  replace them with independently owned copies first (e.g. with
  X509_STORE_CTX_set_chain for the chain).

