+// SSL_new_peer_chain_verify_ctx returns a new |X509_STORE_CTX| set up to
+// verify |ssl|'s peer certificate chain exactly as the built-in verification
+// does: the same verify store, default purpose, verify parameters and ECH
+// name override. Returns NULL, queuing no error, if a verify callback is set
+// on |ssl|, its |SSL_CTX|, or the verify store (any of these may use |ssl|
+// and so cannot run where the result might be used), or if there is no peer
+// certificate chain yet; other failures return NULL with an error on the
+// queue. As with |X509_STORE_CTX_init|, the result only borrows |ssl|'s
+// current store and chain: replace them (e.g. with
